menu "ISO Virtual Media: HTTP API (P8 / C-12)"

    config ISO_ENABLE
        bool "Enable the ISO virtual media HTTP API (/api/v1/iso*)"
        default n
        depends on SD_ENABLE
        help
            Register /api/v1/iso* (upload, list, mount, eject, delete) on the main HTTPS server
            (docs/WEB_API.md section 8, docs/ISO_MOUNT_DESIGN.md). When disabled, the paths are not
            registered (404).
            The API answers 503 not_ready until the SD / MSC glue (A-13, A-14) calls web_iso_set_env().
            TODO(A-14): add "&& USB_MSC_ENABLE" to the dependency when the USB MSC option exists
            (docs/ISO_MOUNT_DESIGN.md section 8: ISO_ENABLE depends on both).

    config ISO_OP_LOCK_WAIT_MS
        int "iso_op_mutex wait limit of an HTTP handler (ms)"
        default 20
        range 1 1000
        depends on ISO_ENABLE
        help
            A mutating request waits at most this long for iso_op_mutex, then answers
            503 {"error":"busy"} with Retry-After: 1 (the single-threaded httpd must not be held by the
            worker's long steps). docs/ISO_MOUNT_DESIGN.md section 4.1.

    config ISO_PUT_RECV_TIMEOUT_S
        int "Receive deadline of one PUT chunk (s)"
        default 2
        range 1 30
        depends on ISO_ENABLE
        help
            One chunk must be received within this time; otherwise nothing is written and the
            connection is closed (the /ws input must not be stalled). Used by the PUT receive loop
            (TODO(A-15), docs/ISO_MOUNT_DESIGN.md section 6.1).

endmenu
